{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "FR-142-AC-27 to FR-142-AC-30, FR-322-AC-301 and FR-322-AC-302 (TC-187 U41 to U44, TC-280 MU-31 to MU-34): the carried quantity type `Quantity<u, C>` (`scalar_type`/`carried_quantity`) and its conversion. `nodes` lists the nodes of one importing package `example` by key; a path segment `{\"node\": key}` is the structural id of the node `key` (the path of FR-322 \"Derived type forms and forwarding\"). `wire` holds CQ-W01 to CQ-W14: the shape and conversion-application cases, each `admitted`, `distinct` (two nodes with different paths) or a refusal with `code`, `cause` and the node `at`. `evaluation` holds CQ-E01 to CQ-E16, the exact halves of TC-187 U07, U08, U16, U17, U18 and U29 and the precedence case U43: each names the `source` value, its `unit`, the `target` carrier node, the mode (always `exact`: the nearest-even halves of U07, U16 and U29 are unchanged and not restated), the optional `limits` tuple `L(i,d,e,o,w,r)` of TC-187 as a list `[integer_bits, decimal_digits, unit_edges, value_occurrences, work_units, result_units]`, and the `expected` disposition. The reader and evaluator that decide these outcomes are quire-contract-ir's and quire-verification's; the vectors are authoritative for them and QSpec's test checks only their shape and that each `completed` or `refused` outcome follows from the exact value and the carrier.",
